    "turn_text": "You know, I'm not sure I got invited to go to the meeting and, you know, I'm always open for a conversation and, you know, I don't have any real ambition at this point, you know, to do anything. I'm here to serve the caucus. I ran last time. I obviously stated my case and, you know, I mean, we'll see what happens. However, the caucus thinks I can be helpful. I'll be helpful. I got invited to, I don't know, share my opinions, which I think are pretty clear and have been since November of what I think of the current circumstances that are going on with the House Democratic Caucus. And, you know, unfortunately, you know, being, you know, oh and for against Trump and Trump candidates is disconcerting to a lot of us and, you know, what makes us kind of a little bit leery as we go into the 2018 cycle with more races, so I think that's going to be on everybody's mind as well.",
