    "turn_idx": 90,
    "turn_text": "Well, I'm not saying it can't be done. It can be done. I'm just saying that I think it does provide a good solid impediment to us potentially getting there. And the Republicans have spent a lot of money damaging her over the last 10, 11 years, really muddying her up and making her a very polarized figure in our politics today. That's reality. I mean, there's a reason they're still running these ads. If you don't think that's true, then why are they running these ads? And why are they winning races where they're running these ads? And why do Republicans grab us Democrats and say, please don't make a change with House leadership? We like things just the way they are. Why were they hanging support Pelosi sign out of their headquarters in November during the election? There's a reason for it. And so it's not personal against leader Pelosi. It's just reality in our caucus. You know, had an opportunity in November to make a decision. And I'm not saying I'm going to be all end all. I'm just saying make them spend a couple hundred million dollars damaging somebody else that they can tie to our candidates, but",
