    "turn_idx": 96,
    "turn_text": "Well, I don't know I mean I you know you're you're hearing a lot of grumblings But I don't know what level with that I mean that's again the decision the caucus has to make and I say that because you know I went through this where there was a lot of grumblings in November a lot of people thought we needed to change course and No one else was running, so I put my hat in the ring to offer an alternative, and we got a third of the votes, which I thought was pretty good in the fact in the course of a couple of weeks. Now what that number is now for somebody else who would may want to do it, or if her support has eroded, I have no idea. But the caucus has to make a decision. One way or the other, I think, is if we're going to go into 2018 with the current leadership that we have, or are we going to try to make a change and if people are willing to do that publicly to make that change, to try to improve our chances in 2018, the caucus has to make that decision and that means that every individual member has to say You know, it's not about",
