    "turn_text": "I think it's totally possible. You know, I'm not ruling out the possibility of that happening. I mean, Trump is, you know, I think continuing to betray the people who put him in office. He's not got the economy going. You know, he said he was going to open up steel mills and coal mines and really get people back to work. That's not happening. His budget. decimates a lot of investments that would help working class people and obviously the health care bill is throwing people off a health care when he said he was going to expand medicare medicaid and make it more affordable uh... for people inaccessible to people in the complete opposite he hasn't really gotten any past yet but the the house bill certainly does and it sounds like the senate bill isn't that far off presenting that to the american people in contrast with what he said during the campaign what they've done you know i still think we have an opportunity to do that but You know, I come out of, like, athletics. It's like you get yourself in the absolute best position to win. And, you know, to me, that means addressing the issue we have with this national brand and figuring out how to do creative things with our campaigns that are going to, you know, take the energy that's on the ground now, which is really significant and exciting, and try to channel that into elections. like with the OSOP race, you know, we're not going to have 20, 25 million to spend in races like that. Right. You know, we're not going to have that kind of money. So if you're not going to win it when you're spending 25 million bucks and you've rallied the entire country around it, you know, it gets hard to say, okay, how are we going to put 40 or 50 of these seats in play when we don't have 25 million dollars for each of these races?",
